From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 23:00:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libfakekernel: add `lowbit64()` to match `highbit64()`

`libfakekernel` defines `highbit64()` but not `lowbit64()`, although the kernel
provides both and callers reasonably expect the pair. Add it, and export it from
the mapfile.

Found packaging `zpool` for a cross build: `libzpool` cannot be built here
because its Makefile wants `dtrace -h`, so `zpool` links `-lfakekernel`
instead -- and the only things it wanted from `libzpool` were `highbit64()` and
`lowbit64()`. The link runs under `-zdefs`, so if that ever stops being true it
fails at build time rather than at run time.

Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5 (claude-opus-5)
---
 usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/kmisc.c      | 43 +++++++++++++++++++
 usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/mapfile-vers |  2 +
 2 files changed, 45 insertions(+)

diff --git a/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/kmisc.c b/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/kmisc.c
index 70f303e035..812fe8b2ed 100644
--- a/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/kmisc.c
+++ b/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/kmisc.c
@@ -60,6 +60,49 @@ ddi_get_pid(void)
 	return ((pid_t)getpid());
 }
 
+/*
+ * Find lowest one bit set.
+ *	Returns bit number + 1 of lowest bit that is set, otherwise returns 0.
+ */
+int
+lowbit64(uint64_t i)
+{
+	int h = 64;
+
+	if (i == 0)
+		return (0);
+
+	if (i & 0x00000000ffffffffULL)
+		h -= 32;
+	else
+		i >>= 32;
+
+	if (i & 0x0000ffff)
+		h -= 16;
+	else
+		i >>= 16;
+
+	if (i & 0x00ff)
+		h -= 8;
+	else
+		i >>= 8;
+
+	if (i & 0x0f)
+		h -= 4;
+	else
+		i >>= 4;
+
+	if (i & 0x3)
+		h -= 2;
+	else
+		i >>= 2;
+
+	if (i & 0x1)
+		h -= 1;
+
+	return (h);
+}
+
 /*
  * Find highest one bit set.
  *	Returns bit number + 1 of highest bit that is set, otherwise returns 0.
diff --git a/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/mapfile-vers b/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/mapfile-vers
index 5082db903e..327db57de0 100644
--- a/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/mapfile-vers
+++ b/usr/src/lib/libfakekernel/common/mapfile-vers
@@ -187,6 +187,8 @@ SYMBOL_VERSION SUNWprivate_1.1 {
 	kstat_waitq_to_runq;
 	kstat_runq_back_to_waitq;
 
+	lowbit64;
+
 	msec_per_tick;
 
 	mutex_owned;
